{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBIteratedLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBIteratedLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBBranchPointSum","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogReflection"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.wp1_outer_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.wp1_outer_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBIteratedLimit.lean#L248-L264","doc":"**OUTER limit (`ρ → 1⁻`) of the iterated-limit route.**  The INNER bulk value\n`Li₂(x) − Li₂(ρ)` (the limit of `wp1_bulk_tendsto` for each fixed interior `ρ`)\ntends to the W-P1 target `Li₂(x) − π²/6` as `ρ → 1⁻`, by the sorry-free Abel /\nleft-continuity brick `tendsto_LiTwo_nhdsWithin_lt_one` (`Li₂ → π²/6`).  Composing\nwith `wp1_bulk_tendsto` realises the **iterated limit**\n\n`lim_{ρ→1⁻} lim_{q→1⁺} −(1−q)·Σ_{k<n(q)} log(1−xqᵏ)  =  Li₂(x) − π²/6`,\n\nthe W-P1 target, with **no Diophantine input**.  (Combined with W-P2, the\nDedekind-eta asymptotic of `DilogPartBEulerTail`, this gives the Part-B total\n`reg_n → Li₂(x) − π²/3` under the iterated ordering.  The iterated limit is a\n*weaker* statement than the joint `q→1⁺ × n→∞` limit, whose unconditional pointwise\nform is proved-false; see the coordination ledger.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.wp1_bulk_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.wp1_bulk_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBIteratedLimit.lean#L142-L246","doc":"**INNER bulk closure of Dilog Part B W-P1.**  For fixed `x ∈ (0,1)` and a fixed\n*interior* target `ρ ∈ (x,1)`, with the bulk floor index `n(q) = ⌊log(ρ/x)/log q⌋`,\nthe positive-factor rescaled log-sum converges to the interior dilog difference\n\n`−(1−q)·Σ_{k<n(q)} log(1−xqᵏ)  ⟶  Li₂(x) − Li₂(ρ)`   as `q → 1⁺`.\n\nProof: `wp1_riemann_bound` gives `0 ≤ (Li₂(xq^{n}) − Li₂ x) − (1−q)Σ ≤ E(q)`.  The\ndilog difference `→ Li₂(ρ) − Li₂ x` (endpoint `x q^{n(q)} → ρ` by\n`tendsto_nOfQ_mul_pow`, then continuity of `Li₂` at the interior `ρ`).  The majorant\n`E(q) = (q−1)(−log(1−xq^{n})) − (q−1)q^{n}(−log(1−x)) → 0` because both boundary\nfactors stay **bounded** away from the branch point (`x q^{n} ≤ ρ < 1` and\n`q^{n} ≤ ρ/x`), so the width `q−1 → 0` kills them — **no Diophantine input**.  Hence\n`(1−q)Σ = (Li₂(xq^{n}) − Li₂ x) − [error ∈ [0,E]] → Li₂(ρ) − Li₂ x`, and negating\ngives `Li₂(x) − Li₂(ρ)`.  This is the INNER limit of the iterated-limit route; the\nOUTER `ρ → 1⁻` limit (`Li₂ x − Li₂ ρ → Li₂ x − π²/6`) is the Abel brick\n`tendsto_LiTwo_nhdsWithin_lt_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_nOfQ_mul_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_nOfQ_mul_pow","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBIteratedLimit.lean#L124-L140","doc":"**Clean endpoint limit (INNER, bulk).**  For `0 < x`, `x < ρ`, `ρ < 1`, the endpoint\n`x · q^{n(q)}` converges to `ρ` as `q → 1⁺`.  Squeezed between `ρ/q → ρ` (lower,\n`nOfQ_mul_pow_gt`) and the constant `ρ` (upper, `nOfQ_mul_pow_le`).  The absence of\noscillation — the whole point of the bulk route — is visible in the `ρ/q` lower\nenvelope tending to `ρ` cleanly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.nOfQ_mul_pow_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.nOfQ_mul_pow_gt","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBIteratedLimit.lean#L90-L122","doc":"**Lower endpoint bound.**  For `0 < x`, `x < ρ`, `1 < q`:  `ρ/q < x · q^{n(q)}`.\nFloor gives `log(ρ/x)/log q < n(q) + 1`, so `log(ρ/x) − log q < n(q)·log q`, hence\n`q^{n(q)} = exp(n(q)·log q) > exp(log(ρ/x) − log q) = (ρ/x)·(1/q) = ρ/(x q)`, so\n`x q^{n(q)} > ρ/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.nOfQ_mul_pow_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.nOfQ_mul_pow_le","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBIteratedLimit.lean#L62-L88","doc":"**Upper endpoint bound.**  For `0 < x`, `x < ρ`, `1 < q`:  `x · q^{n(q)} ≤ ρ`.\nFloor gives `n(q) ≤ log(ρ/x)/log q`, so `n(q)·log q ≤ log(ρ/x)`, hence\n`q^{n(q)} = exp(n(q)·log q) ≤ exp(log(ρ/x)) = ρ/x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.nOfQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.nOfQ","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBIteratedLimit.lean#L56-L60","doc":"The **bulk floor index** `n(q) = ⌊log(ρ/x)/log q⌋₊` — the largest `n` with\n`x qⁿ ≤ ρ` when `1 < q` and `x < ρ`.  Unlike the branch-point index\n`⌊log_q(1/x)⌋`, the target `ρ` is *interior* (`ρ < 1`), which is what makes the\nendpoint limit oscillation-free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}